[Music]  well more than 2 300 nevadans will be  diagnosed with breast cancer this year  but a new test could dramatically  shorten their treatment  and could revolutionize cancer treatment  worldwide  the theralink test is designed to map  out the exact  treatment needed to fight a specific  type of cancer it's really  groundbreaking stuff  and it's being tested right here in  southern nevada here's today's health  watch  i think this would just answer a lot of  my  questions and my doubts staring down  cancer can give anyone pause  anika vallejo is a mother of three and a  stage one breast cancer patient  she's agreed to a groundbreaking new  test being conducted at comprehensive  cancer centers  she's the first in the world to receive  theralink  it's not often in las vegas that we get  the opportunity to be the first in  anything  and so she is really the first patient  to receive this test  the molecular test analyzes various  proteins on a cancerous cell  and then determines which proteins are  turned on or  off this is part of something called  precision oncology  and what precision oncology does is  we're trying to find the right p  with the right drug for the right  patient at the right time  now typically oncologists prescribe a  first line of treatment  if that doesn't work then a second line  and eventually a third  no matter what kind of treatment you get  just always kind of wonder  is this the right one should i be really  doing this dr schwartz hopes theralink  will remove a lot of the guesswork  i can see a future in the near future  where  every cancer patient gets this type of  testing molecular testing of the tumor  because it really gives doctors more  information about what the right  treatment is  for patients it could be a path that's  less invasive  and more accurate so we are going to be  following aniko's journey and bring you  updates on her progress

